{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>I will not see your face again.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: 'I am not coming to you; you are coming to me.' And this is what it says: ״וירדו כל עבדיך אלה אלי״ — 'all your servants shall come down to me.' It should have said וירדת — 'you shall come down' — but he paid honor to royalty and attributed the coming down to his servants, though he himself came down to him from his palace at night, in the manner of what is written: ״ויקם פרעה לילה הוא וכל עבדיו״ and so forth, ״ויאמר קומו צאו מתוך עמי״." "<b>And behold.</b> According to this utterance — what he said to him, ״עוד נגע אחד אביא על פרעה בהיכלו״ — the Shekhinah was revealed to him there, and there the utterance came to him. And the reason was that Moshe said to him ״לא אוסיף עוד ראות פניך״ — so that he not be found a boaster, the Shekhinah was revealed to him in that very place. And this is what our Rabbis of blessed memory said: 'The Elohim, as it were, sprang upon him — entered the palace of Pharaoh — for the sake of Moshe, who had said ״לא אוסיף עוד ראות פניך,״ so that he not be found a boaster.' You find that the Holy One, blessed be He, did not speak with him in Pharaoh's house except at that hour, of which it is said (Exodus 9:29): ״כצאתי את העיר אפרוש את כפי אל ה'״ — and now the Holy One, blessed be He, sprang forth and spoke with Moshe, as it is said: ״עוד נגע״ and so forth."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:44.310480163Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}